course: dictionary
lesson: 13130
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the sentence around the word. «Followers» is a good example: it can mean people who support a leader, or people who see your posts online.
explain: «The young captain had many loyal followers who believed in her plan.» Here followers are people who support and believe in the captain. Now read this: «Mia's video got a thousand new followers in one day.» These followers are people who choose to see Mia's posts online. The words video and day are your clues.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The ducklings were followers, walking in a neat line behind their mother.» Followers here means animals that come after someone. Does your meaning still make sense? If yes, you have found the right one.
fact: Followers means more than one follower.
fact: «Followers» can mean people who support a leader, team or idea.
fact: On social media, «followers» are the people who choose to see your posts.
fact: «Followers» can also mean people or animals that come after someone.
fact: Safety: never share personal details, such as your address or school, with online followers you don't know.
exercise: «The team has thousands of loyal followers who cheer at every match.» What are the followers here? | *People who support the team and cheer for it | Shops that sell the team's kits | Players who score the goals | Referees who blow the whistle
exercise: «Maya posted a photo, and her followers liked it.» What are Maya's followers? | Animals that walk behind her | Her teachers at school | Photos that she has taken | *People who choose to see her posts
exercise: Ahmed says a follower is always a copycat. Is he right? | Yes, a follower only copies | *No, a follower can support a leader, a team or an idea | No, because followers are always animals | Yes, but only online
test: «The explorer's followers walked through the snow behind her.» What does followers mean here? | Dogs that guard the camp | *People who go after or come behind her | Posts that she shared online | Mountains she climbed
test: Lily asks, «Should I tell my followers online where I live?» What is the safe answer? | Yes, because followers are always friends | Yes, if they have many likes | Yes, but only at night | *No, never share personal details with online followers you don't know
exam: «Jack has a thousand followers online, and his friends are proud of him.» What does followers mean in this sentence? | People who support a team | Animals that come behind Jack | *People who choose to see Jack's posts on social media | Leaders who make the rules
